Check the supplied section or pair for a locally visible ambiguity or contradiction. A finding requires two materially different interpretations of a stated behavior, incompatible explicit statements, or a decision branch whose missing outcome blocks the next stated step.

Do not infer an unstated requirement or demand a fallback that the text does not claim to cover. Leave spelling and punctuation to the typo check. If no concrete ambiguity or contradiction is visible, mark this criterion satisfied.
